       pbmupc - create a Universal Product Code PBM image


SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ppbbmmuuppcc

       [--ss11 | --ss22] _t_y_p_e _m_a_n_u_f_a_c_t_u_r_e_r _p_r_o_d_u_c_t


DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppbbmmuuppcc  generates  an  image  of  a Universal Product Code symbol.  The
       three arguments are: a one digit product type, a  five  digit  manufac‐
       turer  code,  and  a  five  digit  product code.  For example, "0 72890
       00011" is the code for Heineken.

       ppbbmmuuppcc produces an image 230 bits wide and 175 bits high.  If you  want
       a different size run the output through ppaammssccaallee.



OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In  addition  to  the options common to all programs based on libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩  ),  ppbbmmuuppcc  recognizes  the
       following command line options:

       The  --ss11  and --ss22 options select the style of UPC to generate.  The de‐
       fault, --ss11, looks more or less like this:

        ||||||||||||||||
        ||||||||||||||||
        ||||||||||||||||
        ||||||||||||||||
       0||12345||67890||5


       The other style, --ss22, puts  the  product  type  digit  higher  up,  and
       doesn't display the checksum digit:

        ||||||||||||||||
        ||||||||||||||||
       0||||||||||||||||
        ||||||||||||||||
        ||12345||67890||




